OL,3,GNEWSATeen receives award for helping
OL,4,Adisabled children
OL,5,
OL,6,FA Kent schoolboy who has a rare genetic
OL,7,Fcondition is set to be honoured with a
OL,8,Fnational award for his efforts to
OL,9,Fimprove the lives of other disabled
OL,10,Fchildren.
OL,12,FGeorge, 15, who has spinal muscular
OL,13,Fatrophy (SMA) Type 2, has campaigned
OL,14,Fand protested alongside the SMA
OL,15,Fcommunity to champion greater inclusion
OL,16,Fand accessibility, a campaign that has
OL,17,Fhelped shape NHS decision-making.
OL,19,FThe Tunbridge Wells teenager said: "I
OL,20,Fdon't want the next generation having
OL,21,Fto fight the same battles. No good ever
OL,22,Fcame from doing nothing."
OL,23,APub: 21-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
